                <pb facs="0728" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-15T02:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1937—2
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Department’s 8, June 14, 6 p.m. Report of revolt inexact or at least
                    premature. [Franco?] appears to be firmly in control. Although there is no
                    outward manifestation thereof there is considerable uneasiness in army circles
                    as well as among populace over Chaco situation <pb facs="0729" n="719"
                        xml:id="pg719"/> which is so involved with internal political conditions
                    that any conjecture as to the outcome would be premature at this moment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
